{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"indigoid-endemic-shrimp","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\n`docs/config.md` cites obsolete ADR numbers for cross-ticket overlap and transport retry. It also says `REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW` was removed, while `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` and focused tests still read it as an enabled-by-default diagnostic switch.\n\n## Plan\n- Point cross-ticket overlap guidance to ADR 0086.\n- Point transport retry guidance to ADR 0087.\n- Describe `REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW` as an active diagnostic switch and state its current default and false-value behavior.\n- Preserve the distinction between diagnostic snapshot composition and behavior-bearing configuration.\n- Change Markdown only and do not alter the switch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Cross-ticket overlap and transport retry links resolve to ADR 0086 and ADR 0087.\n- [x] The shadow switch is documented as active, diagnostic, and enabled by default.\n- [x] False spellings and invalid-value behavior match `shadow_enabled()`.\n- [x] No source, test, or configuration behavior changes.\n- [x] Targeted documentation index and link checks pass.","id":"c0d7-4b47-a0ac-40d4","parent_id":"86a1-7944-8c43-4010","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F19C correct configuration decision and diagnostic guidance"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788160596988009001,"uuid":"354ef53a-2fa7-4951-92fe-03b165f1f9aa"}